  <section number="12.4" title="Integration of Trigonometric Functions">
    <subsection title="Integrating Trigonometric Functions">
      <paragraph>
        Each equation pertaining to a rule of differentiation given in Section 12.3 may be integrated to yield a corresponding integration formula. For example, integrating the equation <math display="inline">$$f^{\prime}(x) = \cos x$$</math> of Rule 1 with respect to <math display="inline">$$x$$</math> yields
      </paragraph>
